1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:04,230
One screen. One cut. And the defender never sees it coming!

2
00:00:04,420 --> 00:00:06,070
This is the Shuffle Cut.

3
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:10,330
First, the ball swings to the wing.

4
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:11,830
Now watch the big man.

5
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:14,850
He sets the back screen... right behind the defender.

6
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:16,270
The cutter waits for it.

7
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:18,150
Slow... slow...

8
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:20,530
then he explodes off the screener's shoulder!

9
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:23,640
The defender gets caught chasing, right into the screen.

10
00:00:23,660 --> 00:00:25,530
The wing hits the cutter in stride...

11
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:26,970
and there's your layup!

12
00:00:27,650 --> 00:00:29,760
Screen. Cut. Finish.

13
00:00:29,890 --> 00:00:32,620
That's why timing matters more than just speed.

14
00:00:32,750 --> 00:00:36,080
One screen. Perfect timing. Easy advantage.

